    {
      "id": "top-002",
      "userId": "usr-demo-001",
      "title": "Cellular Respiration: Citric Acid Cycle & Oxidative Phosphorylation",
      "subject": "Biochemistry",
      "content": "# The Citric Acid (Krebs) Cycle\n- **Location**: Mitochondrial matrix.\n- **Starting substrate**: Acetyl-CoA (2 carbons) binds Oxaloacetate (4 carbons) to yield Citrate (6 carbons) via Citrate Synthase.\n- **Yield per Acetyl-CoA**:\n  - 3 NADH (yielding ~7.5 ATP)\n  - 1 FADH2 (yielding ~1.5 ATP)\n  - 1 GTP / ATP\n  - 2 CO2 released\n- **Key Regulators**: Isocitrate dehydrogenase (inhibited by high ATP/NADH; stimulated by ADP/NAD+).",
      "tags": [
        "Biology",
        "Metabolism",
        "Mitochondria"
      ],
