    {
      "id": "top-003",
      "userId": "usr-demo-001",
      "title": "Vector Calculus: Divergence, Curl & Green’s Theorem",
      "subject": "Mathematics",
      "content": "# Fundamental Theorems of Vector Calculus\n- **Green's Theorem**: Relates line integral around closed curve $C$ to double integral over region $D$:\n  $$\\oint_C (L dx + M dy) = \\iint_D \\left( \\frac{\\partial M}{\\partial x} - \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial y} \\right) dA$$\n- **Divergence**: Measure of vector field's outward flux per unit volume: $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F}$.\n- **Curl**: Measure of infinitesimal rotation: $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}$.",
      "tags": [
        "Calculus",
        "Vector Analysis",
        "Physics"
      ],
