    {
      "id": "top-004",
      "userId": "usr-demo-001",
      "title": "Distributed Systems: Outbox Pattern & Idempotency",
      "subject": "System Design",
      "content": "# Transactional Outbox Pattern\n- **Problem**: Dual-write problem when updating SQL database and publishing message to Kafka / RabbitMQ.\n- **Solution**: Save message payload inside an `outbox` table in the same DB transaction.\n- **Debezium / CDC**: Polling publisher or Change Data Capture reads from the outbox and delivers to the event bus.\n- **Idempotency keys**: Cache request keys in Redis with TTL to prevent duplicate processing.",
      "tags": [
        "Architecture",
        "Distributed Systems",
        "Kafka"
      ],
